      "id": "r2",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "गङ्गापारात्, गङ्गामध्यात्. When the last word has the sense of the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "Loc. the final may be changed to अम् as here, the sense being",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "पृष्ठस्य मध्ये. See Gr. § 274. क्रोडाधीन-क्रोड properly means the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "bosom (भुजान्तर see Amara. 11. 77.); hence a portion, a corner,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "of the ocean's surface. क्रोडे अधि क्रोडाधीनं Loc. Tat. The Tad.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "aff. ख (ईन) is necessarily added to a Tat. ending in अधि by",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "Pán. V. 4. 7. अनादरात् with but scanty regard. The ocean seems",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "to take but little notice of the Tortoise with his immense body.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "For the story, see Mat. Pu. Cha. CCXLIX. 26, 27. अहह expres-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "ses here 'wonder, astonishment,' (अद्भुते). निःसीमानः—न विद्यते",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "सीमा यासां. The fem. of निःसीमन् is formed in three ways; so the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "other forms of the pl. are निःसीमाः and निःसीम्न्यः; see बहुराजन्",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "Gr § 329. The fig. in the first three lines is Máladîpaka,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "and in the fourth arthântaranya'sa (confirming the general",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 15,
          "text": "proposition about the magnanimity of the actions of the great",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 16,
          "text": "by the particular instance of the sea).",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 36. मघवन्—Indra. The word here may be मघवन् or",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "मघवत्; मंह्यते पूज्यते इति मघवा or—वान्. The former is derived by",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "'श्वन्नुक्षन्—Un. I. 159; the latter by 'मघवा बहुलम्' Pán. VI. 4. 128.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "तुषाराद्रेः सूनुः—Maináka, son of Himàlaya and Mená. Cf. असूत सा",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "नागवधूपभोग्यं मैनाकमम्भोनिधिबद्धसख्यम् । क्रुद्धेपि पक्षच्छिदि वृत्रशत्राववेदनाज्ञं",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "कुलिशक्षतानाम् Kum. 1. 20. Allusion-Formerly the mountains had",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "wings with which they flew about and grew very troublesome.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "To stop the evil Indra lopped off their wings with his thunder-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "bolt when hundreds of them flew to the sea for protection.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "Only Maináka escaped the fate which overtook others. For this",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "legend, see Rámâ. Sun. K. Adh. I. 115–119. For the physical",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "explanation, see Notes on Rag. 1. 68. Mark the use of the word",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "उचित here. In the construction of वरम् न च or न पुनः, such a word",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "is not usual, its signification being implied in the construction",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 15,
          "text": "itself. Mr. Telang's note.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 37. यत्-तत्—since then; in as much as. पादैः स्पृष्टः- ( 1 )",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "touched with the rays; ( 2 ) with feet. तेजस्वी—of pre-eminent",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "valour. विन् showing excess ( भूमन् ) 'अस्मायामेधास्रजो विनिः Pán V",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
